target:    wp-slimstat.php
gate:      php tests/subsite-table-hook-test.php
kind:      name-only
expect:    does not delegate to the Schema manifest
rationale: table() interpolates the name itself while a comment still says Schema::tableName() — the tenth-creator shape (C11) with the manifest's name left behind as prose. The gate strips comments and strings before matching, so the comment must not save it: unvalidated interpolation returns a plausible name for ANY typo and fails at query time instead of call time.
---
diff --git a/wp-slimstat.php b/wp-slimstat.php
--- a/wp-slimstat.php
+++ b/wp-slimstat.php
@@ -2330,7 +2330,8 @@
      */
     public static function table($name, $blog_id = 0)
     {
-        return \SlimStat\Schema\Schema::tableName($name, self::get_blog_prefix_for($blog_id));
+        // Schema::tableName($name, ...) semantics, inlined for speed:
+        return self::get_blog_prefix_for($blog_id) . $name;
     }

     /**
